    "detailedExplanationEn": "🎯 Correct Answer: Option D (\"The beneficial impact of a calibrated light exposure protocol on sleep recovery\")\n\n• Audio Evidence & Breakdown:\nThe clinical trial demonstrates that phototherapy (\"blue-enriched white light at ten thousand lux for thirty minutes\") before bedtime recalibrates melatonin cycles, generating a 45% boost in daytime sleep quality for night-shift healthcare workers.\n\n• Detailed Distractor Breakdown (Incorrect Options & Refutations):\n  - Option A (Abolition of overnight hospital shifts) [INCORRECT - UNREALISTIC LEAP]: The trial seeks to mitigate fatigue among essential night workers, not shut down emergency healthcare wards.\n  - Option B (Superior efficacy of synthetic sedatives) [INCORRECT - COMPLETE OPPOSITE]: Phototherapy is championed specifically as a drug-free physiological circadian intervention.\n  - Option C (Banning nurse smartphone screens) [INCORRECT - SCREEN TIME RED HERRING]: The report makes no reference to prohibiting handheld devices during daytime hours.\n  - Option D (Beneficial light protocol impact) [CORRECT]: Accurately reflects the documented 45% improvement in daytime restorative sleep and cognitive alertness."
